# Forward Architecture Cutoff (July 2026)

**Canonical spec:** [docs/architecture/FORWARD-ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/architecture/FORWARD-ARCHITECTURE.md)  
**Slice layout detail:** [vertical-slice-modularity.mdc](vertical-slice-modularity.mdc)  
**Arkitect intake:** [arkitect-mcp-paved-route.mdc](arkitect-mcp-paved-route.mdc)

## Cutoff (2026-07-05)

**Modular Vertical Slices + Legacy Facades** — ship first, no big-bang rewrite.

| Forward (new logic) | Legacy (extract only on touch) |
|---|---|
| `extension/popup/features/<feature>/` | `extension/popup.js` |
| `extension/content/<feature>/` | `quick-paste/quick-paste.js` |
| `extension/background/handlers/`, `messaging/` | Root shims until facaded |
| `extension/supabase/*.js`, `extension/shared/` | Pre-cutoff ad-hoc roots |
| **`extension/bridges/<domain>/`** — ACL | `extension/popup.html` inline CSS (strangler via UI phases) |

## Arkitect complement (clean-slice-fusion)

| Arkitect ID | PasteCraft role |
|---|---|
| **vertical-slice** | Feature folders own UI + orchestration |
| **modular-monolith** | Single MV3 zip; strict internal boundaries |
| **strangler-fig** | Replace legacy only when edited |
| **anti-corruption-layer** | `extension/bridges/*` translates legacy ↔ slice |
| **clean-slice-fusion** | Inward dependency direction inside slices |

**Patterns at seams:** Facade + Adapter (`bridges/`), Command + Mediator (background router), Strategy (site/sync adapters), Decorator (wrap legacy during migration). **Deferred:** CQRS, event sourcing, microservices.

## Bridge rules

1. Slices **never** import legacy monoliths — one facade per domain in `extension/bridges/<domain>/`.
2. Facade owns ID normalization, sync queue, storage quirks; ≤10 exports per domain.
3. Cross-context: `message-types.js` + router — not ad-hoc strings.
4. **Extract on touch:** facade first → slice extract → shrink legacy.

## CRUD (forward code)

- Server IDs only (`session.user.id`, Postgres `gen_random_uuid()`).
- Writes through facades / services — RLS by `auth.uid()`.
- No custom RLS plumbing (`set_config`, device_id query filters).

## Forbidden

- New business logic in monolith files or growing `popup.html` JS.
- Cross-slice imports; mass `extension/legacy/` moves.
- Auto-refactor without explicit migration intent (Arkitect policy).

## Agent default

Arkitect paved route → implement on `main` until SUCCESS → task branch commit. CodeScene on changed files.
